						"question": "Are over-ear headphones comfortable for extended periods of listening?",
						"answer": "<p><strong>Yes, over-ear headphones are generally comfortable for extended periods of listening</strong>, especially when they are well-designed. They fully enclose your ears, which helps distribute pressure more evenly around the head and reduces ear fatigue compared to on-ear or in-ear options.</p><p>However, comfort can vary depending on head shape, weight of the headphones, and how tight the clamping force is. Trying them on or reading user reviews can help you find a pair suited for long sessions.</p>"
					}
				},
				"tab-2": {
					"type": "tab",
					"settings": {
						"question": "Do over-ear headphones offer better sound quality compared to in-ear models?",
						"answer": "<p><strong>Yes, over-ear headphones often offer better sound quality compared to in-ear models</strong>, especially in terms of soundstage, clarity, and bass response.</p><p>Here’s why:</p><ul><li><strong>Larger drivers</strong> in over-ear headphones can produce richer, more dynamic sound.</li><li><strong>Better soundstage</strong> gives you a more immersive, \"live\" experience, with clearer separation between instruments.</li><li><strong>Improved bass response</strong> due to more space for air movement.</li><li><strong>Noise isolation or cancellation</strong> tends to be more effective in premium over-ear designs<br/></li></ul><p>However, high-end in-ear monitors (IEMs) can also deliver excellent sound quality, especially for studio use or travel, and are often more portable. So while over-ears generally have the edge for audiophile or home listening, the best choice depends on your use case.</p>"
					}
				},
				"tab-3": {
					"type": "tab",
					"settings": {
						"question": "Are over-ear headphones suitable for sports or gym activities?",
						"answer": "<p>Over-ear headphones are generally not ideal for sports or gym activities. While they can offer excellent sound and comfort, they come with a few drawbacks for active use:<br/><br/><strong>Why they may not be suitable:</strong></p><ul><li>Bulky and heavier than in-ear models, which can feel cumbersome during movement.</li><li>Less stable fit, making them more likely to shift or fall off during intense activity.</li><li>Limited sweat resistance — most over-ear headphones aren’t designed to handle moisture or heat buildup.</li></ul><p><strong>Better alternatives:</strong></p><ul><li>In-ear (true wireless or wired) earbuds with secure fit options (ear hooks, wings).</li><li>Sweatproof or waterproof ratings (IPX4 and above) are recommended.</li><li>If you really prefer over-ears for the gym, look for sport-specific models designed for durability and moisture resistance — but for most people, in-ears are the more practical choice.</li></ul>"
					}
				},
				"tab-4": {
					"type": "tab",
					"settings": {
						"question": "How do I maintain and clean my over-ear headphones?",
						"answer": "<ol><li><strong>Unplug or turn off the headphones</strong><br/>Always disconnect them from your device before cleaning to avoid damage.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Wipe down surfaces</strong><br/>Use a soft, dry or slightly damp microfiber cloth to clean the headband, ear cups, and exterior. Avoid harsh cleaners or alcohol.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Clean the ear cushions<br/></strong>If they’re removable, take them off and gently wipe with a damp cloth.<br/><br/>For deeper cleaning, use a mild soap solution and let them air dry completely before reattaching.<br/><br/>Leather or faux leather pads benefit from a light application of conditioner.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Clean the mesh/grill (speaker area)</strong><br/>Use a dry, soft-bristled brush or cotton swab to remove dust or debris gently—don’t press too hard.<br/><br/></li><li><strong>Check for sweat or moisture buildup</strong><br/>After workouts or long sessions, wipe down immediately to prevent material breakdown or odor.</li></ol>"
					}
